      "strategyID": "strategy-memo:33be555c211916cff4a9c97624ac6617b41342c181e7abb4c79b8206c9054423",
      "strategyText": "I write as Brock, approaching my authored first encounter with the inventory, identity and evidence you have provided.\n\nMy roster is finite and locked: Geodude at level 12 with Effect Nightmare, Defense Curl and two vacant slots, and Onix at level 14 with Effect Nightmare, Bind and Rock Tomb. No acquisition is available; no items, moves or species may be added. The preparation envelope confirms two active companions, zero healing items and a move-change budget of two, which I may distribute only within the existing move sets. My signature attachment to Onix is strong, and I intend to retain that bond while using the budget to optimize the moves I already have.\n\nThe social evidence I have is limited to a single reported battle and a Pok\u00e9mon-seen post, both from trainer:fr:trainer:0102, sourced from pokebook. A repeated report from one original source is not independent corroboration, and I do not treat it as such. The battle outcome was favorable to the reporter, and the species seen was Bulbasaur, but I cannot infer a pattern or predict the next opponent from this alone. I accept uncertainty about the unseen player party, unannounced moves and the order of future actions.\n\nMy strategy proceeds from caution and resource conservation. I will lead with Geodude, using Effect Nightmare to apply pressure early, then shift to Onix to leverage Rock Tomb for coverage and Bind for sustained control. I will pace setup patiently, accept that the next opponent and their party are unknown, and rely on the moderate aggression and caution baked into my behavioral reference. I do not select a candidate move, switch or item beyond what is legally present; I simply execute the roster I have, preserving my original companions and signature lineage."
    },
