      "strategyText": "# Memo: Authored First Encounter\n\nTrainer identity: Confident and direct, matter-of-fact style. This engagement is my authored first encounter in the early-Kanto ordinary sequence. I enter without new levels, companions, or supplies.\n\nRoster composition: Two baseline partners at level 10\u2014Rattata and Nidoran F. Each carries four moves with two unoccupied slots (marked NONE). Rattata knows Effect Nightmare, Effect Atk Plus 2, and Quick Attack. Nidoran F knows Effect Evs Plus 2, Effect Uproar, and Effect Atk Plus 2. No held items. Resource conservation is strong; zero healing items available.\n\nEvidence inventory: Two reported posts from trainer:fr:trainer:0414 describing battle 034e8d9... with native outcome 1. One reports a TRAINER_BATTLE_RESULT; the other a POKEMON_SEEN claiming Bulbasaur was seen. Source quality is MODERATE. I treat these as attributed reports, not independent corroboration. A repeated report from one original source carries no additional weight. I do not know the unseen player party, unannounced moves, future actions, or opponent party composition.\n\nPreparation envelope: Acquisition allowance is zero. Active capacity is two\u2014the current roster. Eligible origins are empty. Move-change budget stands at two. Level targets are fixed at 10 for both companions. Origin weights favor native (0.8) over nearby (0.2). Reserve capacity is zero. Stage is first.\n\nTactical intent: Pressure with existing partners. I will operate within the constraints of my authored roster\u2014two level-10 baseline Pok\u00e9mon with limited move sets and no healing items. I acknowledge uncertainty in opponent composition and outcome prediction. Decisions will be made against the known facts: two allies, zero external acquisition, and the reported but unverified evidence of prior encounters. I preserve original companions and accept that imperfect plans are part of this first encounter."
